properties.description:
Why is there not a traffic signal at this incredibly dangerous intersection?  Coming from South Boundary, in order to make a left onto Country Club road, in traffic, which is getting worse, and not in traffic, one must navigate many dangerous circumstances:
1. Traffic from Battle Lane often not respecting the stop sign to take turns; 
2. Traffic from country club rd making a right to Battle lane, often speeding, and often not using a turn signal;
3. Traffic from country club rd making a right to S. Boundary, often speeding and often not using a turn signal;
Then, when you've made it past the first stop sign to the triangle to make a left, one has to navigate more dangerous situations, not only for the driver, but also pedestrians and bikers:
1. Traffic making a left from country club rd either onto Boundary or Battle; 
2. Traffic on Country Club heading to 54;
3. Traffic coming from 54 and headed to either Boundary, Battle, or Cameron.
Then one has to be aware of Pedestrians crossing, at their own peril, nonetheless, as well as bikers biking in non-protected lanes.  

And this is all just for one car trying to make a left from south boundary.  This is truly mind bogglingly dangerous and unacceptable!  What is the reason for this? Why are safer solutions not being implemented?
